Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against jin-s13/xtcocoapi]

get_version() only returns version.py's short_version when 'sdist' or
'bdist_wheel' is in sys.argv, and otherwise falls back to __version__, which
version.py does not define. That else branch is dead code under upstream's
own usage (always a literal `python setup.py sdist`/`bdist_wheel`), but a
modern pip first calls prepare_metadata_for_build_wheel with 'dist_info' (not
'bdist_wheel') in sys.argv, hitting the else branch and raising
KeyError: '__version__'. This is why the manylinux_riscv64 cp313/cp314/cp314t
legs fail at the metadata-prep step while cp312 (whose image ships an older
pip that skips straight to bdist_wheel) does not; it is not riscv64-specific
and reproduces with any sufficiently new pip on x86.

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -7,7 +7,9 @@ def get_version():
         exec(compile(f.read(), version_file, 'exec'))
     import sys
     # return short version for sdist
-    if 'sdist' in sys.argv or 'bdist_wheel' in sys.argv:
+    # pip's build backend also runs prepare_metadata_for_build_wheel with
+    # 'dist_info'/'egg_info' in sys.argv, not 'bdist_wheel'; treat the same.
+    if {'sdist', 'bdist_wheel', 'dist_info', 'egg_info'} & set(sys.argv):
         return locals()['short_version']
     else:
         return locals()['__version__']
